1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,120
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,577
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,897
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:55,717
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
Then I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,300
We'll live in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,097
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We'll live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
But we don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,777
But we have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,480
We live in one another.

26
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:57,980
Whoa, look at that!

27
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,480
Tears are making a rainbow!

28
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:05,580
The film is crying, we'll drown here!

29
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:07,486
It's practically a waterfall.

30
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:08,940
So sad!

31
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:10,900
Master Froggy!

32
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,920
Ahhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh!

33
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,030
Ahhhh!

34
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:19,290
Ahhhhh!

35
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,100
Ahhhhhhhhhh!

36
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:25,210
Ahhhhhhhh!

37
00:02:25,293 --> 00:02:26,420
Ahhhhhhh!

38
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:30,650
Ahhhhhhhh!

39
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:31,563
Dory!

40
00:02:31,646 --> 00:02:32,476
You're alive!

41
00:02:32,559 --> 00:02:33,787
I must've lost consciousness

42
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,157
Mr.

43
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,070
Zero

44
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,977
I've heard that name somewhere before.

45
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:47,817
Wasn't that the name of the boss
guy that Vivi was so frightened of?

46
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:53,160
Which would mean that the person who was
on the other end of this transponder scale

47
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,260
is one of the seven warlords of the sea.

48
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:03,817
It's been a long time since
I issued your orders, Mr.

49
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:04,730
Three.

50
00:03:04,813 --> 00:03:06,342
What's happening on that island?

51
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,960
All right, so I guess this Mr.

52
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:12,315
Three character is the owner
of this transponder snail.

53
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,558
I think I have this figured out now.

54
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:18,640
This little place here is an enemy
hideout, and someone named Mr.

55
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,497
Three was ordered by someone named Mr.

56
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:23,580
Zero to come to this island
and kill Vivi. Damn it!

57
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,997
What was I thinking?

58
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:28,017
This was no time for me to
be out on a hunting trip.

59
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:30,159
I hope that they're all still okay.

60
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:31,170
Shit.

61
00:03:31,253 --> 00:03:33,121
Well, are you going to answer me?

62
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:35,931
When I ask a question, I expect an answer.

63
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:40,077
Have you eliminated Princess Phoebe
and the Straw Hats as you were ordered?

64
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:40,990
Oh, yeah.

65
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,797
The mission was successful.

66
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:45,717
I eliminated all those pesky
brats like you said to.

67
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,337
Your secret is completely protected,

68
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:51,780
so there's no need to keep going
after them anymore. I see. So,

69
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:53,420
as we speak,

70
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,477
the Unluckies are headed your way in order
to confirm the success of your mission.

71
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:59,537
And to deliver a certain package.

72
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:01,780
The unluckies, of course.

73
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:02,980
And a package?

74
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:06,947
It's an eternal pose that will
point you to Alabasta Kingdom.

75
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:11,897
Once that arrives, you and Miss
Golden Week will head for Alabasta.

76
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:14,392
It's time for the next phase of the plan.

77
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:19,532
We are about to begin, embarking upon
our most important operation to date.

78
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:22,117
Details will follow
after you reach Alabasta.

79
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,318
Wait for my orders.

80
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,310
What the?

81
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,282
What are those?

82
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,310
Mr.

83
00:04:33,393 --> 00:04:34,340
Three, what was that?

84
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,620
Oh, uh, it's nothing, really.

85
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,494
What the hell is that?

86
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:57,917
So I guess you're trying to kill me, huh?

87
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,529
Well, monkey, bring it on!

88
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,620
All right, you, what now?

89
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:16,020
So what are you going to do
now, you oversized chicken?

90
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:24,240
Hey, what's going on?
Answer me, Mr. Three.

91
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:27,200
Hey, well, nothing.

92
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:28,737
It's just...

93
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:31,140
that damn Straw Hat was still alive.

94
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,619
It's okay, though.

95
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:34,337
I finished him off real good.

96
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:35,420
No need to worry.

97
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,940
What do you mean, he was still alive?

98
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,737
I believe that just a moment ago you said

99
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:45,257
that your mission was
completed successfully.

100
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:46,458
Isn't that correct?

101
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,720
Yes, that is what I said.

102
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:52,634
I mean, I absolutely thought
that it was completed then,

103
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:56,544
but that Straw Hat guy is really
a lot tougher than you'd expect.

104
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,400
So let me see, if I understand.

105
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:02,191
The report you gave me was a complete lie?

106
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:03,900
Well, yeah.

107
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:07,097
When you put it that way, I guess
the report wasn't the truth.

108
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:10,077
But, now I've gotten rid
of that Straw Hat for sure,

109
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:14,336
so there's no need for you to send
anyone else after him or the others.

110
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:15,430
Very well.

111
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:19,177
Take the pose and head straight to
Alabasta from there immediately.

112
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:20,495
Do you understand me?

113
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:23,360
But, how are you still alive?

114
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,120
The weapons.

115
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,600
They saved me.

116
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:29,030
Weapons?

117
00:06:29,113 --> 00:06:29,943
Oh, yeah!

118
00:06:30,026 --> 00:06:30,957
That makes sense!

119
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:33,357
Not even weapons that were made
in Elbath could hold up after

120
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,717
a hundred years of giants
dueling to the death with them!

121
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,360
They must be dull by now!

122
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,360
Now that's a relief.

123
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:42,920
It's a miracle, really.

124
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:47,080
Broggy, would you let go?

125
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:48,657
I'm a little sore here.

126
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:52,280
I'm so glad you're still
alive, Dorry! It's amazing!

127
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:59,420
Come on, this wasn't a miracle.

128
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:01,957
The fact that those weapons
are even intact after

129
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,137
a century of fighting
is the miraculous part.

130
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:05,577
They should be scrapped by now.

131
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:07,778
I'm surprised they lasted this long.

132
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:10,100
What a day this was!

133
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:13,104
Thank you, god of Elbat,
for this wonderful day!

134
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:14,090
Oh?

135
00:07:14,173 --> 00:07:15,280
Is that true, Broggy?

136
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:17,477
You're saying that fighting
me while I was injured,

137
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:20,736
Cutting me down and knocking
me out was all wonderful.

138
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,217
Don't be an idiot, Dory.

139
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:24,771
That's not what I'm saying and you know it

140
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:27,253
Would you keep your hands off my wounds?

141
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:39,062
You try doing that again
and see how far you get?

142
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:42,160
I can take you down in a heartbeat!

143
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:48,530
Wait!

144
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,897
You two are fighting again already?!

145
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:55,500
We'll have no more radio
contact from now on, understand?

146
00:07:55,940 --> 00:08:00,137
If the Marines were to catch on to what
we're doing, that would be most unfortunate.

147
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:01,137
From this point on,

148
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:05,037
all of my orders will be sent via
letter, following the usual protocol.

149
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,355
That will be all, Mr.

150
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:07,290
Three.

151
00:08:07,373 --> 00:08:08,489
Good luck on your mission.

152
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:18,740
Miss Allsunday.

153
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:20,940
Yes, sir?

154
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:22,560
I want you to send Mr.

155
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:24,661
Two to Little Garden immediately.

156
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:26,590
Mr.

157
00:08:26,673 --> 00:08:29,117
Three is on his way from
Little Garden to Alabasta.

158
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,553
I want you to see that he is eliminated.

159
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:36,180
Perhaps that might be a
little extreme, Crocodile.

160
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:39,320
We still have plenty of agents to spare.

161
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,073
Are you arguing with me, Miss Allsunday?

162
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:43,710
No.

163
00:08:43,793 --> 00:08:45,359
I'll make the arrangements at once.

164
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:46,500
Consider it done.

165
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:51,700
Well, he finally hung up.

166
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,700
Now, I wonder who these guys were.

167
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,567
They sure are funny looking.

168
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:03,480
What's this?

169
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:09,446
Captain Smoker, I've just
intercepted a very intriguing signal.

170
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,200
What is it?

171
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:16,377
Such an incredible full temper.

172
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:18,840
The legendary Kashi!

173
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:20,760
Tashigi! Tashigi!

174
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:26,600
Only here in the Grand Line could I find
such a prized sword as this so quickly!

175
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,640
Tashigi! Come here!

176
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:30,180
Are you dead?

177
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:32,446
Yes, they're coming, Captain!

178
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:40,834
Stop clowning around and get over here!

179
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,686
I need you to listen to this!

180
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:44,500
Listen close.

181
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:47,337
We just picked up this
conversation minutes ago.

182
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,497
I've got it all queued up.

183
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:50,500
Ready, Sergeant Major? Uh, yes.

184
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:53,140
Lay it back, please. It's Mr. Zero.

185
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,576
Now quit fooling around, you jackass.

186
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:59,037
Have you eliminated Princess Phoebe
and the Straw Hats as you were ordered?

187
00:09:59,120 --> 00:09:59,950
Straw Hats?

188
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:01,900
Straw Hat Pirates! Oh, yeah.

189
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:03,611
A mission was successful.

190
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:05,360
From this point on,

191
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:09,441
all my orders will be sent via
letter following the usual protocol.

192
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:10,797
That will be all, Mr.

193
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:11,710
Three.

194
00:10:11,793 --> 00:10:14,178
And the rest of the message
is undecipherable static.

195
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:15,556
It's a faint signal,

196
00:10:15,660 --> 00:10:17,937
but there are key names and phrases laced

197
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:20,667
in their conversation
that clearly stood out.

198
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:26,380
Princess Vivi, Straw Hats,
Orders via Letter, and Mr. Zero.

199
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:27,920
Mr. Zero?

200
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:30,157
Could that be a codename for somebody?

201
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,070
In fact,

202
00:10:31,153 --> 00:10:32,817
it's quite possible he
could be connected to that

203
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,537
suspicious swordsman we
caught earlier in Rudeness.

204
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:38,100
What did you say his name was? Mr. Eleven?

205
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:39,600
Possibly.

206
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:42,397
Part of a criminal organization that uses

207
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:46,017
numbers for codenames and
sends orders via letter.

208
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:47,159
Sound about right?

209
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:49,050
Huh.

210
00:10:49,133 --> 00:10:50,060
Mr. Zero. Organization.

211
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,871
I have no idea what you're going on about.

212
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,577
Then how do you explain the letter of
detailed orders we found in your pocket?

213
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:58,600
Damn letter!

214
00:10:58,780 --> 00:10:59,817
I thought I burned it!

215
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:00,730
Wait!

216
00:11:00,813 --> 00:11:02,360
That's not... not mine!

217
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,337
That's funny.

218
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:07,714
Because we didn't actually
find anything in your pocket.

219
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,637
All right, then.

220
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:18,140
Princess Vivi, if I remember correctly,

221
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:21,637
she's from Alabasta, and reports
say she's currently missing.

222
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:26,217
Excuse me for interrupting, but isn't the
Alabasta Kingdom in the middle of a coup?

223
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:29,197
I wonder if this mysterious
criminal organization and the

224
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:31,897
Straw Hat Pirates could somehow
be involved in the uprising.

225
00:11:31,980 --> 00:11:32,840
Who knows?

226
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:35,617
All I know for certain
is that this is the only

227
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:38,288
clue we have to the
Straw Hat's whereabouts.

228
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:41,440
This means we're going? Yes.

229
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:46,260
I want you to contact headquarters
and get an eternal pose. Yes, sir.

230
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:53,660
It's time we pay a little visit
to Alabasta, the Kingdom of Sand.

231
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:03,098
Gah, gah, gah, gah,

232
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:07,317
We've been fighting so
long that we had completely

233
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:09,817
forgotten about the bounties
that were put on our heads.

234
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:11,312
It has been a long time.

235
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:15,037
But I'm the whole reason that the Baroque
Works agents came here in the first place.

236
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:15,950
It's my fault.

237
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:18,880
None of that anymore, okay?

238
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:20,157
Yeah, come on, Phoebe.

239
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,358
Why are you so sad?

240
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,557
Here, have a rice cracker.

241
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:24,470
Uh, guys?

242
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,720
Where did you get those? I know.

243
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:28,722
Let's have a rice cracker party.

244
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:30,537
Rice crackers aren't
that exciting, though.

245
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:31,740
Sure they are!

246
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:33,037
We can even toast with them!

247
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,885
You see, nobody's blaming you.

248
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,570
Cheers!

249
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,230
Ow!

250
00:12:38,313 --> 00:12:39,549
Hey, Luffy, don't do that!

251
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,417
Can't just go wasting food like that.

252
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,137
Seriously, you should know better.

253
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:45,632
Hey, what are you doing?

254
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,517
Who said you could have my cracker?

255
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,430
No, put it down!

256
00:12:48,513 --> 00:12:49,343
Can you break it?

257
00:12:49,426 --> 00:12:50,256
It's done!

258
00:12:50,339 --> 00:12:51,169
It's mine!

259
00:12:51,252 --> 00:12:53,000
My nose done! What's with you? Nothing.

260
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:54,281
Just a bug bite.

261
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:55,870
All right.

262
00:12:55,953 --> 00:12:59,417
I still can't believe we have to wait here
a year just for the Log Pose to reset.

263
